  "body": "You see, I want to develop my own chat server using matrix synapse and want to change or modify some features.\r\nAfter following the https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/latest/development/contributing_guide.html guidelines here I am not able to run the software locally for errors. \r\nwhenever I try to run the codebase locally I end up with a error message LIKE :\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n File \"/usr/lib/python3.10/runpy.py\", line 187, in _run_module_as_main\r\n   mod_name, mod_spec, code = _get_module_details(mod_name, _Error)\r\n File \"/usr/lib/python3.10/runpy.py\", line 110, in _get_module_details\r\n   __import__(pkg_name)\r\n File \"/home/yeazin/new_matrix_synapse/synapse/synapse/__init__.py\", line 24, in <module>\r\n   from synapse.util.rust import check_rust_lib_up_to_date\r\n File \"/home/yeazin/new_matrix_synapse/synapse/synapse/util/rust.py\", line 20, in <module>\r\n   from synapse.synapse_rust import get_rust_file_digest\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'synapse.synapse_rust'\r\n```\r\n\r\n \r\nThe error says ModuleNotFoundError : No module named 'synapse.synapse_rust' at the end. \r\n\r\nCan you guys give me some solution on this .\r\n",
